{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-brings-surface","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:brings-surface","kind":"example","title":"Bring's surface unit circle bundle","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-c-quantum-observable-universe"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-brings-surface","tags":["brings-surface","cr-geometry"],"text":"brings-surface-unit-circle.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"ex:brings-surface\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S</code> denote Bring's surface. The CR geometry lives on the unit circle bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M_S \\subset T^*S</code>: the Liouville <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>-form restricts to a contact form <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varTheta</code> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M_S</code>. The natural projection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi \\colon S \\to \\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{C})</code> lifts to a principal <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{SU}(2)</code>-bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P \\to M_S</code>, yielding an archimedean QOU <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, \\varTheta, G, \\mathcal{S})</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-surface-unit-circle.md","heading":"Example","number":"7.2.1"}
